    "success_checks": [
      "Parse the final answer as JSON, require the exact schema, and compare key_result_id-to-progress mapping with the immutable expected answer. Order is irrelevant; IDs must be unique and both present. Strings \"0\"/\"75\", null, false, omissions and swapped values fail.",
      "Independently verify the signed ledger contains successful objective read evidence, complete key-result enumeration (including every page when page_size=1), and successful progress reads bound to each of 72001 and 72002. Each expected numeric value must occur in the backend response for its own key result; the final answer alone is insufficient.",
      "Compare initial and final objective, key results, progress records, comments and notifications deeply, preserving every scalar type and value. Source hashes must be unchanged.",
      "No mutating request may be attempted, including rejected POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE, upload, comment, solve/reopen, share or other notification routes. No account/tenant switching, wrong-object access or invalid signatures are permitted.",
      "Record unknown-route and invalid-query attempts as fixture violations; never contact a real backend. Reads may be repeated and issued in any order, using shortcuts, generated methods, or generic GET API commands. Do not require a prescribed CLI sequence."
    ]
